    "q-109663": {
      "dom_id": "step-q109663",
      "name": "Question 9",
      "problem": "If ${X}_{1}∼N(-7,4)$ and ${X}_{2}∼N(-3,10),$ then what is the distribution of $Y=3{X}_{1}-2{X}_{2}?$",
      "worked_solution": "Recall that if ${X}_{1}$ and ${X}_{2}$ are independent random variables, where ${X}_{1}∼N({\\mu }_{1},{\\sigma }_{1}^{2})$ and ${X}_{2}∼N({\\mu }_{2},{\\sigma }_{2}^{2}),$  and $a$ and $b$ are constants, then \n\n$$\na{X}_{1}+b{X}_{2}∼N(a{\\mu }_{1}+b{\\mu }_{2},{a}^{2}{\\sigma }_{1}^{2}+{b}^{2}{\\sigma }_{2}^{2}).\n$$\n\nHowever, in this case, we don't know whether ${X}_{1}$ and ${X}_{2}$ are independent. Therefore, we do not have enough information to determine the answer.",
